  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...Seasonal and mostly dry weather is expected through \nSaturday.\n\nA cool, northwest flow will support a mix of sun and clouds across \nthe eastern Great Lakes region today. 850mb temperatures have \nlowered to -2C across the region this afternoon. Lake effect \nstreamers continue off Georgian Bay, and this upstream moisture and \ninstability will extend across Lake America this afternoon. Moisture \nremains very shallow across central NY, so only a low chance of rain \nshowers is expected there today. Elsewhere, diurnally driven and \nupslope clouds are expected with sunshine in between.\n\nA surface high will build across the region tonight. Northwest flow \naloft will continue to support some lake clouds, however dry weather \nis expected overnight. Lows will fall into the 30s, low 20s across \nthe higher terrain. \n\nHigh pressure will be in place across the region Saturday. Seasonal \nweather is expected with light winds. \n\nKEY MESSAGE 2...A warming trend is expected Sunday through early \nnext week.\n\nSurface high pressure will move east of the region Saturday night. A \nsoutherly flow will support warmer weather Sunday with highs back in \nthe low 60s. High pressure will move off the east coast early next \nweek, while the westward extent remains across the Northeast. This \nwill support a warm, and dry period through at least Tuesday. \n\nA deep trough is expected to move from the Plains to the Mississippi \nValley by mid-week. There remains high uncertainty in the evolution \nof a surface low and how quick moisture returns to the eastern Great \nLakes region. Chances for showers begin to increase Wednesday with \nthe potential for unsettled weather to continue through the end of \nthe work week. Above normal temperatures are expected mid to \nlate week.",
